{"_meta":{"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://texel/viewer"}},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Apply a patch to a spec (update, replace, add or remove layers by id; change palette, legend or meta) and render the result like texel_render. Layers without an id first get \"<op>-<index>\" and keep it, so the next patch can use the same ids. Entries that cannot apply are skipped and reported. With \"spec\", returns the patched spec, the review and the sheet. With \"file\", writes the patched spec back to that file and returns only the review and the sheet.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"file":{"description":"Instead of \"spec\": a .json spec file in the workspace, e.g. \"skins/knight.json\". Saves resending the whole spec on every call; texel_patch then edits the file in place.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"include":{"default":["sheet"],"description":"Extra outputs. \"sheet\" is the review image; \"ascii\" adds a text render for models without vision.","items":{"enum":["sheet","texture","ascii"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"patch":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"additionalProperties":{},"propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"type":"object"}],"description":"A patch ({ patch: [{ do: \"update\", id, set }, \u2026] }) as a JSON object or JSON text. Format: texel://docs/spec, section \"Patches\"."},"spec":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"additionalProperties":{},"propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"type":"object"}],"description":"A Texel skin spec (version 1) as a JSON object or JSON text. Format: texel://docs/spec, schema: texel://schema/skinspec.v1"}},"required":["patch"],"type":"object"},"name":"texel_patch","outputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"applied":{"type":"number"},"art":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"advice":{"description":"Classic pixel-art mi